    "body": "@Astrantia I haven't had enough time to dig around to figure out whether Arch is alone in not having emoji support in terminals by default. For what it's worth, you most likely would not have seen *any* emojis rendering correctly in your terminal, whether from starship or not, so it's not strictly speaking a starship problem (though you're right in that I should probably add `noto-fonts-emoji` into the suggested packages for the starship AUR packages).\r\n\r\nAs for your question about firefox emojis: I'm not certain. It looks like mozilla provides the font as [fxemoji](https://github.com/mozilla/fxemoji), but I don't know how easy it is to install them and I can't seem to find an AUR provider for those. You might have to build and install it yourself.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
