    "body": "@chipbuster Thanks for doing all that and quick support and I guess this is out of your competence, but for some reason\r\n```\r\n[options]\r\nfont = Twitter Color Emoji\r\nfont = Iosevka Nerd Font 32\r\n```\r\nin `~/.config/termite/config` doesn't seem to force my termite to render Twitter Emojis. \r\nI had installed noto emojis and JoyPixels before I installed ttf-twemoji-color, and even though I had `Twitter Color Emoji` indicated in the config, the terminal was still displaying `Noto Emoji` emojis. I then uninstalled Noto Emojis with pacman and the terminal started displaying JoyPixels. I then uninstalled JoyPixels and now terminal's displaying some emoji that are not twitter emoji. Is there a way to force Termite to display Twitter Emoji Color? This has been frustrating me too much, and these emoji are really important when using Starship :(\r\n\r\nThis is what I'm seeing now \r\n![test](https://i.imgur.com/TPEO69s.png)\r\n\r\nI bet these are not Twitter Color Emoji, but I've set Termite font to `Twitter Color Emoji`",
    "author_association": "NONE",
